WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.178
Help articles are full of knowledge that most readers never finish reading.

2
00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:11.387
Turning each task article into a short tutorial means one step becomes one scene,

3
00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:17.442
with the exact screenshot on screen and narration that names every click by its

4
00:00:17.442 --> 00:00:17.902
label.

5
00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:24.358
Start with task articles of three to eight steps on a screen that changes rarely.

6
00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:30.320
Concept pages and settings references do not suit video, but a clear task with a

7
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.811
visible result does.

8
00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:38.526
Each scene shows the screenshot, a slow zoom, and a sentence that says what to click

9
00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:40.205
and where to find it.

10
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:43.433
Captions are burned in so the video works without sound.

11
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:49.122
When the interface changes, update the article and its screenshots, then re-render.

12
00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:54.776
The article stays the source of truth, and the written steps stay below the video so

13
00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:57.603
readers can still scan and copy from them.
